WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.180
My next guest has appeared in such films

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.600
as "Soul Plane" and
"John Tucker Must Die."

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.420
Now she can be seen in the
new movie, "The Grudge 2,"

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:08.320
let's take a look.

00:00:09.194 --> 00:00:11.861
(wood creaking)

00:00:16.157 --> 00:00:18.657
(eerie music)

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:30.557
(girl crying)

00:00:33.415 --> 00:00:36.082
(wood creaking)

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:42.100
(girl screaming)

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:45.897
Please!

00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:47.522
Please!

00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:49.250
(screaming)

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.083
Oh, man.

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.010
(audience applause)

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.170
That's pretty intense.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.457
Please welcome Arielle Kebbel!

00:00:54.457 --> 00:00:56.940
You know, all the time on this show,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:59.190
we're showing clips of
like a frightening movie,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.600
and it's not that frightening.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.100
That's a really scary
piece of film right there.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.820
Well thank you, I'm glad it's scary.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.770
Your scream is very impressive.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.210
Thank you.
That's a good scream.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.043
Thank you.

00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.300
Did you know you could scream like that

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.660
when you got this part?

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.493
Not quite like that.

00:01:13.493 --> 00:01:16.063
I've never quite really had
a ghost coming at me before.

00:01:16.063 --> 00:01:16.896
[Conan] Right.

00:01:16.896 --> 00:01:18.300
So that was the first time for that.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:20.120
But no, I grew up in Orlando, Florida,

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.900
home of every theme park-

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.733
[Conan] Right.
and you know,

00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:23.870
before I was doing TV and film,

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.320
I spent a lot of time as an
extra, riding roller coasters.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.153
As an extra?

00:01:28.153 --> 00:01:30.050
Why would they need
extras on roller coasters?

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:31.957
Because not everyone
actually wants to go on them

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:33.600
(Conan laughing)
like in the commercials.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.590
Really? So you were-
Sorry Disney, Universal,

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.603
and Sea World.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:39.568 --> 00:01:41.160
So like for commercial or something,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.640
they'd put you on a rollercoaster.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.473
Oh yeah.

00:01:43.473 --> 00:01:45.010
And they make you ride it like 32 times.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.670
[Conan] Right.
In fact, they only stop

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.847
if you're puking or feel
like you might puke.

00:01:48.847 --> 00:01:50.270
[Conan] Right, right.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:51.430
So my friends and I,

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:52.330
I was like 14 at the time,

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:53.800
so we thought it was really cool

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.190
if we actually started
feeling sick riding it,

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.240
so we'd try and outdo each other.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:01:59.750
We'd ride it like 10 times at a time.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.060
But yeah, that's where, you know...

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.990
The camera, you get more camera time

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.560
if you look scared and
you've got, you know,

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.520
your teeth are showing

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.650
and you're loud.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.190
And so I let loose screaming
back then and it paid off.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.023
That's great.

00:02:12.023 --> 00:02:12.856
Yeah, 'cause I was...

00:02:12.856 --> 00:02:14.170
That's one of the things
that grabbed my attention

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:15.610
when we were watching these clips today

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.910
and just you, that's an amazing scream.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.200
You can use that, you know?

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.033
Thank you.
Yeah.

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.270
If I could scream like that,
I'd be doing it all the time.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.103
Like down the streets

00:02:23.103 --> 00:02:23.950
of New York?
My scream does not impress.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:25.580
Mine is more like, "No!"

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.657
You know?
(audience laughs)

00:02:26.657 --> 00:02:28.910
Or like, "Ah!"
Ah, look out!

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:29.800
You know?

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.960
It's free turn of the century.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:31.980
It's not good.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.863
Beware!

00:02:34.178 --> 00:02:35.220
You should be in "Grudge 3."

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.053
Yeah, yeah-
They'd love that.

00:02:36.053 --> 00:02:37.260
that would be great, yeah.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:39.690
Me, hiding from the monster.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:40.740
No, ghost, go away, ah!

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.540
Please, ghost, flee!
(audience laughs)

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:45.860
Am I pronouncing your name right?

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:46.693
It's "Arielle."

00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:47.810
Is that right?
Arielle.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.643
Arielle Kebbel.

00:02:48.643 --> 00:02:49.800
And you actually got "Kebbel" right too.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.870
How do you mess up "Kebbel?"

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.117
It's K-E-B-B-L-E, it's not like,

00:02:53.117 --> 00:02:54.440
"Kooblah? Kahblah?"

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.273
You know what?

00:02:55.273 --> 00:02:56.220
You might want to talk to some people

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.340
because they've messed it up.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.780
You're one of the first
that's gotten the right.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.780
I'm amazed at how many
people over the years,

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:02.647
when I was a kid especially,

00:03:02.647 --> 00:03:03.847
"Conan," it just always seemed like,

00:03:03.847 --> 00:03:04.977
"Well, that's pretty obvious."
"Connan?"

00:03:04.977 --> 00:03:06.027
"Connan," "Cronan,"

00:03:06.914 --> 00:03:07.806
"Queenan."
"O'Breen?"

00:03:07.806 --> 00:03:08.639
"O'Brain?"

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:10.210
Well, no. Everyone knows
"O'Brien," it's like...

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.047
(Conan laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:03:11.047 --> 00:03:12.760
Sorry.
Sorry.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.142
It's like the only name
in Ireland, you know?

00:03:15.142 --> 00:03:16.340
Okay, I haven't been there.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.430
They had one name. That was it.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.992
So...

00:03:19.992 --> 00:03:21.130
You grew up in Florida,

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:22.150
now you live in Los Angeles.
I do.

00:03:22.150 --> 00:03:24.090
Do you enjoy living in Los Angeles?

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.630
Is it an adjustment from Florida?

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.210
I love it. There's still the palm trees.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.570
There's still the ocean, so that's cool.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.410
I gotta tell you,

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:33.349
Florida does not have
the traffic that the 405

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:34.530
has in LA.
The traffic in Los Angeles

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.053
has gotten terrible.
Oh, unbelievable.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.870
But I think I figured out
a way to deal with it.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:40.703
[Conan] Oh, yeah?

00:03:40.703 --> 00:03:43.190
Okay. Well, it kind of
started not so long ago.

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.230
I used to do this thing
where if I wanted something,

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:48.870
or didn't get my way, or got my way,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:50.300
I would bark like a dog.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.770
And so my...

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.199
I'm just going to nod, like, of course.

00:03:54.199 --> 00:03:55.887
(audience laughs)
(Arielle laughs)

00:03:55.887 --> 00:03:56.870
You mean like you're at a restaurant

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.940
and they bring you mashed
potato, but there's no gravy,

00:03:58.940 --> 00:03:59.942
and you asked for gravy you're like...

00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:02.400
(barking like a dog)
Oh!

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.130
Like that kinda thing?

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:05.960
I don't have rabies, no.
Oh. (laughs)

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:06.793
That's the dog I would do

00:04:06.793 --> 00:04:07.804
it'd have foam coming out the mouth...

00:04:07.804 --> 00:04:08.637
(Conan growling)

00:04:08.637 --> 00:04:10.190
That's great, thanks! Argh!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.000
I'd get a fake paws and wave 'em around.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.290
No, no, no, it's not that bad.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.065
It's just, I would, it's kinda like a...

00:04:15.065 --> 00:04:17.675
(squeaky barking)

00:04:17.675 --> 00:04:18.660
Oh,

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.430
that's pretty good too,
so it's a little dog.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:21.557
Yeah, and it's kinda like a...

00:04:21.557 --> 00:04:24.873
(high-pitched barking)

00:04:24.873 --> 00:04:28.981
(dog begging)
(audience laughs)

00:04:28.981 --> 00:04:29.814
(Arielle laughs)

00:04:29.814 --> 00:04:31.289
This is scarier than the clip somehow.

00:04:31.289 --> 00:04:32.558
(all laugh)

00:04:32.558 --> 00:04:33.391
Now I'm afraid.

00:04:33.391 --> 00:04:34.224
Apparently,

00:04:34.224 --> 00:04:35.057
(Conan laughing)
that's what my boyfriend said,

00:04:35.057 --> 00:04:36.417
I didn't know that.

00:04:36.417 --> 00:04:37.750
You do this to your boyfriend?

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:39.330
I do, but this is, so
this is how it started,

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.530
so for awhile, I think he probably thought

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:41.363
it was really weird,

00:04:41.363 --> 00:04:42.196
but he kind of,

00:04:42.196 --> 00:04:43.200
I guess you got used to it

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.270
and now, we've done this thing,

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:47.400
we both do it now, so he's gonna kill me,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.670
but when you're in traffic,

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.670
it's more healing than any yoga,

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.540
than any drink, than anything you can do-

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:55.340
Right and you're getting tense.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:57.100
You're getting tense,
someone cuts you off,

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.930
you've got that urge to just yell at 'em

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.470
or just flip 'em off or whatever.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:03.041
Instead, you roll down your
window and you just go...

00:05:03.041 --> 00:05:04.970
(growls ferociously)

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:06.400
Okay, that would get you killed

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.008
so fast.
(audience laughing)

00:05:08.008 --> 00:05:08.841
You know that, don't you?

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.674
To me,

00:05:09.674 --> 00:05:11.920
that seems worse than
giving someone the finger

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.230
or waving a gun at them, going...

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.234
(growling fiercely)
Think about it.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.084
Think about it!

00:05:15.084 --> 00:05:15.917
You've got your head out the window,

00:05:15.917 --> 00:05:17.970
and someone's totally
expecting you to yell at them

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:20.280
and instead you just growl like (growls)

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.410
and they don't know, they're like...

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.570
[Conan] That's so weird.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.520
They kinda twitch a bit

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.590
and they don't know whether
to laugh or cry, you know?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.550
I do a variation, which
is I hiss like a cat,

00:05:28.550 --> 00:05:29.750
I go (hisses) like that.

00:05:30.866 --> 00:05:32.000
See, that's a little more scary to me,

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:32.880
but that's not loud enough.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:34.030
If you're in traffic,
they have to hear you.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.052
You got to get it like right here, like...

00:05:36.052 --> 00:05:37.320
(growling aggressively)

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:38.590
That'd be so weird if we had ever met

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:39.969
like at a singles club and you were like

00:05:39.969 --> 00:05:40.802
(vicious barking)

00:05:40.802 --> 00:05:42.507
and I was like (hissing)

00:05:42.507 --> 00:05:43.520
It was this weird,

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.400
kinda crazy kinda-
We're like

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.660
petting each other.
I wouldn't do that.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:47.670
Well, actually I would do that,

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.504
yeah.
Yeah, see?

00:05:48.504 --> 00:05:49.337
I know, there you go.

00:05:49.337 --> 00:05:50.943
Like, I draw the line
there. That's getting weird.

00:05:50.943 --> 00:05:52.560
Okay.
What we were doing before

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.743
was perfectly normal.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:56.685
Well, "The Grudge 2" is in theaters now.

00:05:56.685 --> 00:05:58.977
Today, Friday the 13th.
Today, so check it out.

00:05:58.977 --> 00:05:59.981
I hope we scare you.
And Arielle Kebbel,

00:05:59.981 --> 00:06:00.814
thank you so much.

00:06:00.814 --> 00:06:01.647
[Arielle] Thank you so much.

00:06:01.647 --> 00:06:03.297
Nice hissing and growling at you.

